                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "513241c7-9a88-4bae-a83e-a48de01e3613",
                        "source_entry_id": "849d0374-c092-3bea-95b2-016235b17c72",
                        "source_sense_id": "c8ba4026-d2f5-3c5c-972f-59fd1bbab18f",
                        "source_sense_description": "mit drei vervielfacht; zweimal und ein weiteres Mal; dreifach vorgekommen, durchgeführt",
                        "target_lang_word": "three times",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "159adaf9-ae41-4cc7-a4d9-398c8f91cfda",
                        "source_entry_id": "849d0374-c092-3bea-95b2-016235b17c72",
                        "source_sense_id": "c8ba4026-d2f5-3c5c-972f-59fd1bbab18f",
                        "source_sense_description": "mit drei vervielfacht; zweimal und ein weiteres Mal; dreifach vorgekommen, durchgeführt",
                        "target_lang_word": "thrice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "thrice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22497aaf-a298-3b7f-93e7-3b2b444467df",
                                        "entry_id": "f9f8c3a5-a46a-312c-9b93-cc0cfff83c14",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Three times."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "Canada",
                                            "New-Zealand",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d52129a8-e44d-46d2-b63d-364bbd6885fe",
                                                "sense_id": "22497aaf-a298-3b7f-93e7-3b2b444467df",
                                                "text": "Thrice ore the caddow I mine armes outſpred: / Thrice did I fall, before I once could riſe: / Leaning vpon mine elbow for a reſt, / Nodding, I knockt my chin againſt my breſt. // Then ſigh’d, ſlipt downe, and twixt the ſheete and pillow / I nuzled in, joyn’d knees and chin together: / I dream’d I wore a garland of greene willow. / But ſnuffling low, I prickt me with a fether; / So wakt, the bolſter for my backe I choſe, / And yawning thrice, I rub’d mine eyes and roſe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "454c6f2b-e811-499f-9363-51d0f6930338",
                                                "sense_id": "22497aaf-a298-3b7f-93e7-3b2b444467df",
                                                "text": "The weyward Siſters, hand in hand, / Poſters of the Sea and Land, / Thus doe goe, about, about, / Thrice to thine, and thrice to mine, / And thrice againe, to make vp nine, / Peace, the Charme’s wound vp."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ec534ff-7e5a-4cca-9456-a1ea8e8de0d0",
                                                "sense_id": "22497aaf-a298-3b7f-93e7-3b2b444467df",
                                                "text": "And the second time the cocke crew : and Peter called to minde the word that Jesus ſaid unto him, Before the cocke crow twiſe, thou ſhalt denie me thriſe. And when he thought thereon, he wept."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc892e17-c8ee-4344-9c2c-92af6d36b88c",
                                                "sense_id": "22497aaf-a298-3b7f-93e7-3b2b444467df",
                                                "text": "How far might I have been on my way by this time! I am made to tread thoſe ſteps thrice over, which I needed not to have trod but once: Yea, now alſo I am like to be benighted, for the day is almoſt ſpent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b53b26b-f5de-4280-b1a4-8ab5b3cc94f5",
                                                "sense_id": "22497aaf-a298-3b7f-93e7-3b2b444467df",
                                                "text": "Once, twice, thrice, I met Young Lubin on the Green, / once, twice, thrice, Young Lubin he met me, / the firſt time I beheld the Lad he made a humble bow, / I bluſh'd and hung my ſilly head and felt I don't know how, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbf0c381-79f7-4e0e-9828-749fe4955ab7",
                                                "sense_id": "22497aaf-a298-3b7f-93e7-3b2b444467df",
                                                "text": "Roger Wildrake, also, who had twice or thrice put to his eyes what remained of a kerchief, interested by the lady's evident distress, though unable to comprehend the mysterious cause, hastened to assist the divine in supporting so fair a burthen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1848d17f-4650-4fd4-abd2-bff7f7bd18b0",
                                                "sense_id": "22497aaf-a298-3b7f-93e7-3b2b444467df",
                                                "text": "And then he [Bedivere] threw the sword into the water as far as he might, and there came an arm and a hand above the water, and met it and caught it, and so shook it thrice and brandished. And then the hand vanished away with the sword in the water."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2a7ff9c-0fbc-41b8-8244-89e38d00dd75",
                                                "sense_id": "22497aaf-a298-3b7f-93e7-3b2b444467df",
                                                "text": "Seven hours after giving birth […] Kate [Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge] gave the world a first glimpse of their third child, a new Prince of Cambridge. […] Minutes after the brief photocall, the couple headed home with William [the Duke of Cambridge] emerging with his son in a car seat and holding Kate’s hand. “Thrice the worry now,” a smiling William said, holding up three fingers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56fcc322-864b-47d7-9945-0f139c99e2c8",
                                                "sense_id": "22497aaf-a298-3b7f-93e7-3b2b444467df",
                                                "text": "In his young Major League career, Paul Skenes has thrice pitched at least eight innings. In those three outings, he allowed a total of four runs and struck out at least eight batters all three times."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
